<!--
  Fixture: real-shaped institutional XML from the clearinghouse feed.
  PHI removed at the adapter boundary per spec §2.1 — patient, insured, MRN,
  PCN, and provider identifiers are stripped or neutralized. Everything the
  §8.0 gate and §9 adjudication consume is preserved verbatim.

  Expected outcome: NOT_OPPS. This fixture exists to prove the gate, and it
  trips four of its six conditions independently:

    1. claim_form="ub92"        -> not a recognized outpatient form (§19.22)
    2. type_of_bill="81A"       -> facility type 8, not 13X (§8.0)
    3. rev_code with no proc_code on all 16 lines -> no HCPCS, no SI (§8.0.1)
    4. rev 0110 room & board + value_code 80 = 6 covered days -> inpatient
    5. bill_taxonomy 282NC0060X -> Critical Access Hospital, cost-based (§3.3)
    6. hosp_from_date 2020-08-25 vs CY2026 data -> vintage mismatch (§7.5)

  Also exercises: line id comes from remote_chgid -- present and unique on all
  16 lines here, so lineIdScheme is 'feed', NOT the idx: fallback. (An earlier
  version of this comment said otherwise; it was describing the viewer parser's
  bug of reading `chgid`, not this adapter's output. Fixed per D11.)
  charge_record_type carries the unit qualifier DA vs UN (§19.2); there are no
  per-line dates, so the claim-level date fallback applies.

  total_charge reconciles exactly to the sum of the 16 charge lines (9202.07),
  which the adapter asserts as a cheap input check.
-->
